{"id":"u-69969981-ff49-4b25-90c4-efdde0654228","src":"community","title":"Volume antidote","author":"Ant G.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/blXqnW-untitled-program","desc":"Our goal is:  after proper warm-up pyramid where we stay away from failure, we try to execute our working  sets  as intensive as possible, while staying safe. Focus on \" safe\" first.  \nOne real quallity set pushing further than ever before beats half-assing sets every time. You think you didn't really go all out? Then do another set. But allways have in mind that volume can't replace effort. Focus on \" effort\". \nBarbell movements are mostly 0-1 RIR, but machines are used to go beyond failure. Rest-pause, forced reps... controled negatives, good tempo. Quallity is key.  \nUsing weight that we can lift around 6- 8 times and push it to 12 reps using intensity techniques. \nProgress: we are not focused on \" more\" , we are focused on \" better\".  We need precise execution, control, focus and freshness for every set we do.  Basic tempo \" faster up, slower down\" \n\nSwitching to this program for few weeks could easily lead to fast gains and more weight every session, so, there is no need to bother with when and where to add weight. \nFrequency is based on your recovery. Most of the time,  you will be ready to hit same muscle every 4 days.  This is upper body biased program but it is just example.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-07T08:37:09.317Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8}]},{"n":"Pullover (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":8}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":8}]}